@@ -325,6 +325,186 @@ text = "#cdd6f4"
 
 The active palette is applied in this order: built-in theme, `[theme.custom]`, then `[theme.custom.light]` or `[theme.custom.dark]`. Omitting the mode subtables preserves the existing shared override behavior.
 
+### Theme elements
+
+Palette tokens fan out: `accent`, for example, colors the active tab, popup frames, the focused pane border, and selected rows at once. `[theme.elements]` sits between the palette and the UI as named element slots, like neovim highlight groups. Each slot defaults to exactly what Herdr draws with the active palette, so an empty `[theme.elements]` changes nothing, and theme switches and `auto_switch` keep working. Override one slot without touching the rest:
+
+```toml
+[theme.elements.tab]
+active = { fg = "text", bg = "#222222" }
+inactive = { fg = "subtext0", bg = "panel_bg" }
+
+[theme.elements.pane]
+border_focused = { fg = "#8a8a8a" }
+
+[theme.elements.popup]
+body = { bg = "reset" }
+```
+
+A slot is a table with `fg`, `bg`, `bold`, `dim`, `italic`, and `underline`, all optional. Unset fields keep the slot's default. A color is a palette token name such as `"text"` or `"accent"`, which follows the active theme; `#RGB` or `#RRGGBB`; `"reset"` for the terminal's default color; or `"inherit"` for no color of its own, so whatever is underneath shows through. `bold = false` and the other `false` values turn that attribute off.
+
+Many defaults are written in terms of other slots, and those links follow your overrides. Most `popup` slots take their background from `popup.body`, so `body = { bg = "reset" }` clears the fill of every popup, menu, and the navigator in one line. `pane.title_focused` follows `pane.border_focused`, and the `_custom` tab slots follow their plain counterparts.
+
+`navigator.selected` is patched over the row. With `fg = "inherit"`, the selected row keeps its text, status dot, and meta colors and only changes its background:
+
+```toml
+[theme.elements.navigator]
+selected = { fg = "inherit", bg = "#222222", bold = false }
+```
+
+`herdr config check` reports a color it cannot parse and that field keeps its default. Unknown areas and slots are reported like any other unknown key. Agent state colors (status dots, toast markers, machine status) stay with the palette's state tokens and `[ui.status_icons]`.
+
