 ## UI and sidebar
 
 The sidebar is the main Herdr dashboard. Search `ui.` in the [Config reference](/docs/config-reference/) for sizing, collapsed mode, Agent panel ordering, mouse behavior, pane borders, and other presentation settings.
@@ -355,6 +535,24 @@ Command entries run immediately and then at `interval_seconds` without blocking
 
 Separators appear only between visible entries. Set `tab_bar_right_separator = ""` for direct concatenation. On a narrow tab row, the complete status area yields to the tabs and their controls.
 
+Entries other than `zoom` take an optional `style`, layered over the `tab.status` element, and `padding`, a number of blank cells (0–8) added on each side of the text. Together they make a pill:
+
+```toml
+[ui]
+tab_bar_right = [
+  { type = "command", command = "~/.config/herdr/domain.sh", style = { fg = "panel_bg", bg = "accent", bold = true }, padding = 1 },
+]
+```
+
+Style colors resolve against the client's palette, so token names follow theme switches on every attached client.
+
+`[ui.tab_bar] active_caps` draws two one-cell glyphs in the focused tab's outer padding cells, such as Powerline caps. Each cap is the focused tab's background on the tab bar's background. Tab widths and click targets do not change. Unset draws no caps:
+
+```toml
+[ui.tab_bar]
+active_caps = ["\ue0b2", "\ue0b0"]
+```
+
 ### Outer terminal window title
 
 Herdr emulates the terminals in its panes, so an `OSC 0`/`OSC 2` title written inside a pane stops at Herdr. Herdr writes its own title to the terminal it runs in, which is what window managers and terminal tab bars read:
